INSERT INTO questions (id, lesson_id, license, category, theme, subtopic, difficulty, level, question_fr, question_en, options, options_en, answer_key, explanation_fr, explanation_en, tags) VALUES
('7c900ad7-0000-4000-8000-00007c900ad7', '5af919a6-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a6', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Recalage et transition', 2, 2, 'Pression statique inchangée : 3 200 ft au calage 1020 hPa. Recalage à 1008 hPa avec 27 ft/hPa. Nouvelle indication ?', 'Unchanged static pressure: 3,200 ft at 1020 hPa. Reset to 1008 hPa using 27 ft/hPa. New reading?', '["3 188 ft", "2 930 ft", "2 876 ft", "3 524 ft"]', '["3,188 ft", "2,930 ft", "2,876 ft", "3,524 ft"]', '2 876 ft', 'Variation −12 hPa, donc −324 ft : 3200−324 = 2876. 3524 inverse le signe ; 3188 retire seulement 12 ft ; 2930 utilise dix hPa.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/ppl-met-002.svg)', 'Change −12 hPa, hence −324 ft: 3200−324 = 2876. 3524 reverses the sign; 3188 subtracts only 12 ft; 2930 uses ten hPa.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-002.svg)', '["PPL", "quiz-15-extension", "exam-mcq", "exam-subject:meteorology"]')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET lesson_id = EXCLUDED.lesson_id, license = EXCLUDED.license, category = EXCLUDED.category, theme = EXCLUDED.theme, subtopic = EXCLUDED.subtopic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, level = EXCLUDED.level, question_fr = EXCLUDED.question_fr, question_en = EXCLUDED.question_en, options = EXCLUDED.options, options_en = EXCLUDED.options_en, answer_key = EXCLUDED.answer_key, explanation_fr = EXCLUDED.explanation_fr, explanation_en = EXCLUDED.explanation_en, tags = EXCLUDED.tags;

INSERT INTO questions (id, lesson_id, license, category, theme, subtopic, difficulty, level, question_fr, question_en, options, options_en, answer_key, explanation_fr, explanation_en, tags) VALUES
('7c907f37-0000-4000-8000-00007c907f37', '5af919a6-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a6', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Erreurs et marges sur le relief', 2, 2, 'Dossier fictif joint : 3 100 ft lus avec 1022 hPa, QNH actuel 1010 hPa ; 27 ft/hPa. Assimiler l''altitude au QNH à l''altitude vraie, autres erreurs négligées. Obstacle 2 300 ft AMSL, marge exigée par l''exercice 500 ft. Conclusion ?

![Données du dossier altimétrique](/illustrations/quiz-ppl-met-002-clearance.svg)', 'Attached fictional case: 3,100 ft read at 1022 hPa, current QNH 1010 hPa; 27 ft/hPa. Treat QNH altitude as true altitude, ignoring other errors. Obstacle 2,300 ft AMSL, exercise requires 500 ft clearance. Conclusion?

![Altimetry case inputs](/illustrations/en/quiz-ppl-met-002-clearance.svg)', '["476 ft disponibles, marge de 24 ft", "476 ft disponibles, déficit de 24 ft", "800 ft disponibles, marge de 300 ft", "1 124 ft disponibles, marge de 624 ft"]', '["476 ft available, 24 ft surplus", "476 ft available, 24 ft shortfall", "800 ft available, 300 ft surplus", "1,124 ft available, 624 ft surplus"]', '476 ft disponibles, déficit de 24 ft', 'Recalage : 3100−12×27 = 2776 ft. Au-dessus de l''obstacle : 2776−2300 = 476 ft, soit 24 ft sous le critère. 800 ignore le calage, 1124 inverse sa correction. 500 ft est une consigne fictive de ce cas, pas une règle universelle de survol.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/ppl-met-002.svg)', 'Resetting: 3100−12×27 = 2776 ft. Above the obstacle: 2776−2300 = 476 ft, 24 ft below the criterion. 800 ignores setting; 1124 reverses the correction. 500 ft is this fictional exercise criterion, not a universal overflight rule.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-002.svg)', '["PPL", "quiz-15-extension", "exam-mcq", "exam-subject:meteorology"]')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET lesson_id = EXCLUDED.lesson_id, license = EXCLUDED.license, category = EXCLUDED.category, theme = EXCLUDED.theme, subtopic = EXCLUDED.subtopic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, level = EXCLUDED.level, question_fr = EXCLUDED.question_fr, question_en = EXCLUDED.question_en, options = EXCLUDED.options, options_en = EXCLUDED.options_en, answer_key = EXCLUDED.answer_key, explanation_fr = EXCLUDED.explanation_fr, explanation_en = EXCLUDED.explanation_en, tags = EXCLUDED.tags;

INSERT INTO questions (id, lesson_id, license, category, theme, subtopic, difficulty, level, question_fr, question_en, options, options_en, answer_key, explanation_fr, explanation_en, tags) VALUES
('7c907f38-0000-4000-8000-00007c907f38', '5af919a6-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a6', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Erreurs et marges sur le relief', 2, 2, 'Sans changer de position, 2 600 ft au calage 1000 hPa sont recalés au QNH 1012 hPa. Approximation 27 ft/hPa. Quelle indication au QNH ?', 'Without changing position, 2,600 ft at 1000 hPa is reset to QNH 1012 hPa. Approximation 27 ft/hPa. What QNH reading results?', '["2 924 ft", "2 276 ft", "2 612 ft", "2 870 ft"]', '["2,924 ft", "2,276 ft", "2,612 ft", "2,870 ft"]', '2 924 ft', 'Le nouveau calage est plus élevé de 12 hPa : ajouter 324 ft. L''indication précédente sous-estimait la lecture au QNH actuel ; ce cas est l''inverse d''un calage retenu trop élevé.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/ppl-met-002.svg)', 'The new setting is 12 hPa higher: add 324 ft. The previous indication understated the current-QNH reading; this is the reverse of retaining an excessively high setting.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-002.svg)', '["PPL", "quiz-15-extension", "exam-mcq", "exam-subject:meteorology"]')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET lesson_id = EXCLUDED.lesson_id, license = EXCLUDED.license, category = EXCLUDED.category, theme = EXCLUDED.theme, subtopic = EXCLUDED.subtopic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, level = EXCLUDED.level, question_fr = EXCLUDED.question_fr, question_en = EXCLUDED.question_en, options = EXCLUDED.options, options_en = EXCLUDED.options_en, answer_key = EXCLUDED.answer_key, explanation_fr = EXCLUDED.explanation_fr, explanation_en = EXCLUDED.explanation_en, tags = EXCLUDED.tags;

INSERT INTO questions (id, lesson_id, license, category, theme, subtopic, difficulty, level, question_fr, question_en, options, options_en, answer_key, explanation_fr, explanation_en, tags) VALUES
('7c907f39-0000-4000-8000-00007c907f39', '5af919a6-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a6', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Erreurs et marges sur le relief', 2, 2, 'Au sol : point connu à 700 ft, QNH actuel 997 hPa ; réglage 1007 hPa, indication 970 ft. Avec 27 ft/hPa, quel contrôle est pertinent ?', 'On ground: known point 700 ft, current QNH 997 hPa; setting 1007 hPa, reading 970 ft. Using 27 ft/hPa, which check is relevant?', '["Régler 1017 pour ramener l''indication à 700 ft", "Conclure directement à une panne de capsule", "Conserver 1007 car l''écart est une tolérance démontrée", "Régler 997 puis vérifier une indication proche de 700 ft"]', '["Set 1017 to obtain a 700 ft reading", "Immediately conclude capsule failure", "Retain 1007 because the discrepancy is a proven tolerance", "Set 997 then check for a reading near 700 ft"]', 'Régler 997 puis vérifier une indication proche de 700 ft', 'Réduire de 10 hPa retire environ 270 ft : 970−270 = 700. Vérifier ensuite la tolérance applicable. L''écart seul ne prouve ni une panne ni une tolérance acceptable.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/ppl-met-002.svg)', 'Reducing by 10 hPa removes about 270 ft: 970−270 = 700. Then check the applicable tolerance. The discrepancy alone proves neither failure nor acceptable tolerance.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-002.svg)', '["PPL", "quiz-15-extension", "exam-mcq", "exam-subject:meteorology"]')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET lesson_id = EXCLUDED.lesson_id, license = EXCLUDED.license, category = EXCLUDED.category, theme = EXCLUDED.theme, subtopic = EXCLUDED.subtopic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, level = EXCLUDED.level, question_fr = EXCLUDED.question_fr, question_en = EXCLUDED.question_en, options = EXCLUDED.options, options_en = EXCLUDED.options_en, answer_key = EXCLUDED.answer_key, explanation_fr = EXCLUDED.explanation_fr, explanation_en = EXCLUDED.explanation_en, tags = EXCLUDED.tags;

INSERT INTO questions (id, lesson_id, license, category, theme, subtopic, difficulty, level, question_fr, question_en, options, options_en, answer_key, explanation_fr, explanation_en, tags) VALUES
('7c907f3a-0000-4000-8000-00007c907f3a', '5af919a6-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a6', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Erreurs et marges sur le relief', 2, 2, 'L''altitude GNSS diffère de l''altimètre barométrique correctement calé. Quelle première analyse est justifiée ?', 'GNSS altitude differs from a correctly set barometric altimeter. Which initial analysis is justified?', '["Déclarer systématiquement le GNSS erroné", "Faire la moyenne et l''utiliser comme altitude autorisée", "Comparer les références et les erreurs possibles avant de conclure", "Recaler automatiquement l''altimètre sur la valeur GNSS"]', '["Always declare GNSS incorrect", "Average them and use that as an authorised altitude", "Compare references and possible errors before concluding", "Automatically reset the altimeter to match GNSS"]', 'Comparer les références et les erreurs possibles avant de conclure', 'Les deux systèmes ne mesurent pas la même grandeur de la même manière. Une différence n''identifie pas à elle seule le système défaillant ; une moyenne ne crée ni référence réglementaire ni clairance.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/ppl-met-002.svg)', 'The systems do not measure the same quantity in the same way. A difference alone does not identify a failed system; averaging creates neither a regulatory reference nor a clearance.

![Recalage / Setting change](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-002.svg)', '["PPL", "quiz-15-extension", "exam-mcq", "exam-subject:meteorology"]')
ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET lesson_id = EXCLUDED.lesson_id, license = EXCLUDED.license, category = EXCLUDED.category, theme = EXCLUDED.theme, subtopic = EXCLUDED.subtopic, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty, level = EXCLUDED.level, question_fr = EXCLUDED.question_fr, question_en = EXCLUDED.question_en, options = EXCLUDED.options, options_en = EXCLUDED.options_en, answer_key = EXCLUDED.answer_key, explanation_fr = EXCLUDED.explanation_fr, explanation_en = EXCLUDED.explanation_en, tags = EXCLUDED.tags;

INSERT INTO lessons (id, license, category, theme, title_fr, title_en, content_fr, content_en, difficulty, order_index, level, duration_minutes, tags, learning_objectives) VALUES
('5af919a7-0000-4000-8000-00005af919a7', 'PPL', 'meteorology', 'meteorology', 'Température et humidité', 'Temperature and Humidity', '**Objectif :** À la fin de cette leçon, savoir expliquer et appliquer : humidité et saturation; refroidissement et condensation; exemple d''interprétation.

## Humidité et saturation

![Sur une échelle commune, une température de 12 degrés et un point de rosée de 11 degrés sont séparés de 1 degré.](/illustrations/ppl-met-003.svg)

L''air contient une quantité variable de vapeur d''eau. L''humidité relative compare la quantité présente à la saturation à la même température. Le point de rosée est la température à laquelle l''air devient saturé si on le refroidit à pression sensiblement constante sans changer sa teneur en vapeur. Une petite différence température-point de rosée signale une proximité de la saturation.

## Refroidissement et condensation

Un air qui s''élève se détend et refroidit. S''il atteint la saturation, des gouttelettes ou cristaux peuvent former un nuage. Un refroidissement près du sol peut former du brouillard. L''humidité ne suffit pas seule à prévoir le phénomène : vent, brassage, relief et évolution thermique interviennent aussi. Une inversion peut limiter le brassage et piéger l''humidité.

## Exemple d''interprétation

Une observation donne 12 °C et un point de rosée de 11 °C. L''écart de 1 °C invite à surveiller la visibilité et les nuages bas, surtout si un refroidissement est prévu. Cela ne prouve pas qu''un brouillard existe déjà. Recouper avec les observations, la prévision et l''heure de la journée avant de décider d''un départ VFR.

## Références

- [Météo-France — Guide aviation](https://aviation.meteo.fr/documentation/guide_aviation.pdf)
- [FAA — PHAK, chapitre 12 : théorie météorologique](https://www.faa.gov/regulationspolicies/handbooksmanuals/aviation/phak/chapter-12-weather-theory)

**Support de révision PPL(A).** À faire valider par votre instructeur. Pour un vol réel, utiliser le manuel de l’avion et les publications en vigueur. Les exemples chiffrés sont pédagogiques.', '**Objective:** By the end of this lesson, be able to explain and apply: humidity and saturation; cooling and condensation; an interpretation example.

## Humidity and saturation

![Diagram: Temperature and Humidity](/illustrations/en/ppl-met-003.svg)

Air contains a variable quantity of water vapour. Relative humidity compares the amount present with saturation at the same temperature. Dew point is the temperature at which air becomes saturated if cooled at approximately constant pressure without changing its water vapour content. A small temperature–dew point spread indicates proximity to saturation.

## Cooling and condensation

Rising air expands and cools. If it reaches saturation, droplets or crystals may form a cloud. Cooling near the surface may form fog. Humidity alone does not predict the phenomenon: wind, mixing, terrain and temperature evolution also matter. An inversion can limit mixing and trap moisture.

## An interpretation example

An observation gives 12 °C with a dew point of 11 °C. The 1 °C spread calls for monitoring visibility and low cloud, particularly if cooling is forecast. It does not prove fog already exists. Cross-check observations, forecasts and time of day before deciding on a VFR departure.

## References

- [Reference 1](https://aviation.meteo.fr/documentation/guide_aviation.pdf)
- [Reference 2](https://www.faa.gov/regulationspolicies/handbooksmanuals/aviation/phak/chapter-12-weather-theory)

**PPL(A) revision material.** To be reviewed by your instructor. For an actual flight, use the aircraft manual and current publications. Numerical examples are for training.', 2, 3, 1, 10, '["temperature", "humidity", "dew point", "lapse rate"]', '["À la fin de cette leçon, savoir expliquer et appliquer : humidité et saturation; refroidissement et condensation; exemple d''interprétation."]')
